    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d170">

                <pb facs="0302" n="296" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg296"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rockhill to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 150.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Commissioner of the United States to China</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Peking, China</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1901-08-08"><hi rendition="#italic">August 8,
                                1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In further reference to my No. 115 of June
                    12, last, regarding the erection of expiatory monuments in the foreign
                    cemeteries which were desecrated during the troubles of last summer, I have the
                    honor to inclose herewith for your information copies of certain correspondence
                    between the dean of the diplomatic corps and the Chinese plenipotentiaries, from
                    which it will be seen that this matter has been satisfactorily settled.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d170-a1.xml" xpointer="d170-a1"/>
